WEBVTT

00:27.944 --> 00:32.657
"You must be the change
you wish to see in the world."

00:33.783 --> 00:35.285
That's what Gandhi said.

00:37.704 --> 00:38.705
I…

00:40.457 --> 00:42.834
will create a utopian society.

00:45.462 --> 00:48.214
For all of those
who have fallen into despair,

00:51.885 --> 00:53.386
if we do not have hope,

00:53.928 --> 00:55.555
then we must create it!

00:59.309 --> 01:01.227
This will be the land of hope.

01:02.771 --> 01:03.772
SEASIDE PARADISE
TOKYO

01:03.855 --> 01:07.817
I will make this oasis
into the second Beach!

02:37.657 --> 02:39.492
BEACH

03:16.237 --> 03:17.989
How long are you gonna sleep?

03:21.492 --> 03:23.036
Are you hungover?

03:32.629 --> 03:34.130
Did you get any information?

03:35.340 --> 03:36.758
I'm afraid not.

03:40.720 --> 03:43.056
I think I'd better get up
and get some info.

03:46.476 --> 03:48.645
Seems like Hatter
has taken a liking to you.

03:49.812 --> 03:53.107
You'd better be careful.
The militant corps will be watching you.

03:53.942 --> 03:56.319
And we have no idea
what they're capable of.

04:03.493 --> 04:06.371
I was talking to these guys
who drove all the way to the suburbs.

04:06.454 --> 04:09.332
They were saying that
the further you get from the city,

04:09.415 --> 04:11.334
the crappier and more run-down
the streets are,

04:11.417 --> 04:14.003
and if you keep goin',
it looks like you're actually in a jungle.

04:14.504 --> 04:17.423
They decided they weren't taking
any chances and didn't go any further.

04:17.507 --> 04:18.341
Seriously?

04:18.424 --> 04:22.553
I heard that all the game arenas
are pretty much inside Tokyo!

04:22.637 --> 04:25.181
Come on, people! Who wants to party?

04:27.141 --> 04:30.603
There are rumors about people
who tried escaping the country by boat,

04:30.687 --> 04:33.356
but then those lasers came down
from the sky and killed all of them.

04:33.439 --> 04:34.899
You hear about that?

04:34.983 --> 04:36.109
Hang on a second.

04:36.192 --> 04:41.197
Does that mean that the only people
who are disappearing are in Tokyo?

04:41.281 --> 04:43.449
So, wait.
If this is only happening in Tokyo,

04:43.533 --> 04:46.744
wouldn't the SDF have come to rescue us?
That makes sense, right?

04:46.828 --> 04:48.246
And the fact that they haven't come,

04:48.329 --> 04:50.456
does that mean
that everyone in Japan has disappeared?

04:50.540 --> 04:52.083
The US Army didn't come either.

04:52.166 --> 04:53.626
This is so weird.

04:53.710 --> 04:56.212
Could it be
that the whole world disappeared?

04:57.672 --> 05:00.675
I don't know, man.
I think aliens put chips into our brains

05:00.758 --> 05:02.135
and are playin' with us.

05:02.677 --> 05:04.804
I don't think anyone could escape
from this place.

05:05.805 --> 05:07.223
Gimme a swig.

05:11.144 --> 05:13.313
The more I hear,
the more depressing it gets.

05:14.897 --> 05:16.024
Yeah, I know…

05:16.774 --> 05:19.193
Our only hope might be
with those playing cards.

05:28.453 --> 05:31.497
All right.
I'll head over to the annex now.

05:33.291 --> 05:34.542
Just be careful, okay?

05:35.293 --> 05:37.545
I'll also get food supplies and weapons.

05:37.628 --> 05:40.173
And it'll be great
if I could get a little more information.

05:46.346 --> 05:48.306
Yeah, wouldn't that be real nice?

05:55.438 --> 05:57.899
Hey! You guys mind if I ask you something?

06:01.152 --> 06:02.945
Wait, I'm not trying to hit on ya!

07:13.182 --> 07:15.601
That's what
this utopia really looks like.

07:19.397 --> 07:20.982
Another Beach rule.

07:21.566 --> 07:23.443
"Death if you're a traitor."

07:38.791 --> 07:39.667
Arisu.

07:41.169 --> 07:44.547
You and Usagi seem to have gathered
a whole bunch of information.

07:45.423 --> 07:46.757
Are you two planning something?

07:49.469 --> 07:50.595
No, not really.

07:55.016 --> 07:56.809
All right,
I'll cut to the chase.

07:58.227 --> 08:01.022
How do you think you're going to live
in a world full of despair?

08:02.440 --> 08:03.691
What?

08:15.369 --> 08:17.538
Look, all I want is some answers.

08:19.373 --> 08:21.501
Who's behind these sick games and…

08:23.836 --> 08:26.464
who killed my friends, Karube and Chota.

08:32.220 --> 08:33.971
I thought I'd be able to survive

08:34.680 --> 08:37.308
and go back to the world
the way it used to be.

08:40.228 --> 08:41.896
But if that's not possible,

08:43.064 --> 08:45.608
I want Usagi to return at the very least.

08:47.652 --> 08:49.570
She's the only reason I'm alive.

08:53.032 --> 08:54.325
Very touching.

08:57.995 --> 08:59.163
This wish of yours…

09:00.498 --> 09:01.874
sure is nice,

09:04.252 --> 09:06.170
but not very practical, I'll tell you.

09:08.631 --> 09:13.636
You'd have to win every single game
coming up and become the next Number 1.

09:14.262 --> 09:15.346
Impossible.

09:16.472 --> 09:18.266
Look, it's not about you guys, all right?

09:18.808 --> 09:20.810
We think you both have potential.

09:22.562 --> 09:25.523
- What?
- Yeah, that's why we're here right now.

09:27.650 --> 09:28.818
What do you mean?

09:31.070 --> 09:34.240
What would you say if I told you,
things could play out differently?

09:43.666 --> 09:45.626
Let's go!

09:49.922 --> 09:52.008
They've got a lot of guns.

09:52.675 --> 09:56.345
Their arsenal is in the deepest room
in the annex, and they have patrols too.

09:57.763 --> 09:59.724
As long as they have all those weapons,

09:59.807 --> 10:02.184
Hatter will be in control of everything.

10:08.649 --> 10:09.692
What's the matter?

10:18.034 --> 10:19.201
I'm off!

10:24.165 --> 10:27.460
Hatter's making sure
he keeps control of the militant corps,

10:28.169 --> 10:30.880
but it's only a matter of time
before they retaliate.

10:32.840 --> 10:34.675
And if that happens,

10:35.343 --> 10:38.888
this place will be run
by a bunch of brainless idiots with guns.

10:38.971 --> 10:40.848
Then it's cut and run.

10:42.224 --> 10:43.768
What are you planning?

10:46.854 --> 10:48.939
I'm planning
to steal all the playing cards…

10:50.733 --> 10:52.526
bail off the Beach.

11:02.912 --> 11:04.246
Beach.

11:05.748 --> 11:08.501
A pseudo-utopia
built on one guy's charisma.

11:11.629 --> 11:12.463
But then again,

11:13.798 --> 11:16.467
maybe we're the only ones
who think that way.

11:16.550 --> 11:17.968
BEACH

11:19.512 --> 11:21.305
There is no utopia in this world.

11:23.391 --> 11:24.433
Usagi.

11:26.852 --> 11:28.104
We need to talk.

11:35.444 --> 11:38.698
KABUKICHO

11:38.781 --> 11:40.116
THIS WAY TO THE GAME ARENA

11:55.840 --> 11:56.799
This way.

12:02.430 --> 12:03.889
Kabuki District, huh?

12:05.808 --> 12:06.976
This takes me back.

12:19.780 --> 12:23.284
BEACH

12:23.367 --> 12:24.785
- I can't wait…
- Watch it!

12:24.869 --> 12:26.495
- Hey!
- Excuse me, sorry!

12:40.843 --> 12:43.763
Where the hell is that damn GPS chip?

12:48.434 --> 12:50.603
Okay, so this is where you are!

12:50.686 --> 12:52.188
Did I say you could come in here?

12:54.565 --> 12:56.984
Right.

12:57.067 --> 13:00.696
Something bad has happened.
Ju-- Just come with me, please!

13:01.280 --> 13:02.198
Hurry!

13:08.954 --> 13:10.956
Whoa, what are you doin' here?

13:11.040 --> 13:12.666
What the hell do you two want?

13:13.167 --> 13:14.835
No one asked you to come here!

13:16.003 --> 13:18.297
Actually, I'm the one who asked him.

13:20.382 --> 13:22.718
Yeah? Who says you can summon people now?

13:23.719 --> 13:26.055
There's something important
he has to hear.

13:27.723 --> 13:28.557
Let's go in.

13:31.310 --> 13:32.394
See you later.

13:39.360 --> 13:40.611
What's going on?

13:41.320 --> 13:45.115
Not a clue, but it's gotta be
something pretty serious.

14:28.576 --> 14:30.452
Apparently, he couldn't clear the game.

14:31.245 --> 14:33.789
The maintenance team
just happened to find him in Shinjuku

14:33.873 --> 14:36.000
while we were filling up with gas.

14:39.795 --> 14:42.506
Hey, do me a favor
and keep your hands off him.

14:42.590 --> 14:44.174
You're obsessed with dissecting things.

14:49.221 --> 14:50.764
This is from a bullet.

14:51.348 --> 14:54.059
Did the game he was playing involve guns?

14:54.685 --> 14:56.061
Seems like it.

14:56.145 --> 14:58.814
Apparently, people around the game area
heard gunshots.

14:59.398 --> 15:00.733
Holy shit!

15:00.816 --> 15:03.652
Looks like he should've brought
the militant corps along with him.

15:14.830 --> 15:17.625
So now what? What happens to the Beach?

15:19.209 --> 15:21.295
Nobody says a word about this,
understood?

15:22.004 --> 15:23.547
We don't want people freaking out.

15:25.758 --> 15:28.093
I'll step in as leader since I'm Number 2.

15:28.677 --> 15:30.054
Wait a second.

15:31.639 --> 15:34.516
Shouldn't the strongest person
be the leader?

15:35.809 --> 15:36.769
In case you didn't know,

15:36.852 --> 15:39.480
we're the ones who have been
getting rid of the traitors,

15:40.147 --> 15:42.858
but we've been thrown into the shadows
the whole time.

15:42.942 --> 15:44.860
This bullshit ends now, you got that?

15:44.944 --> 15:46.820
If Number 1 dies,

15:46.904 --> 15:49.782
everyone moves up by a number.
We all knew that.

15:49.865 --> 15:52.701
Yeah, well, this elitist dictator is dead.

15:53.410 --> 15:55.120
The power has shifted, hasn't it?

15:56.246 --> 15:59.416
Let's just be democratic
and go with the majority.

16:01.961 --> 16:05.422
Who's with me and thinks
that Aguni should be our new leader?

16:14.932 --> 16:17.977
Are you all serious right now?

16:19.478 --> 16:20.479
Last Boss.

16:38.205 --> 16:39.832
So I'll ask again.

16:40.541 --> 16:42.751
Who thinks Aguni should be leader?

16:56.682 --> 16:57.599
This…

16:58.183 --> 17:00.060
is not a democracy.

17:01.103 --> 17:03.480
But I think it is, isn't it?

17:05.232 --> 17:07.401
You can vote however you want, right?

17:17.453 --> 17:19.705
And how about
the former Number 2 over there?

17:21.165 --> 17:22.207
What do you think?

17:32.968 --> 17:34.678
And what about you?

17:40.934 --> 17:44.730
Chishiya,
you're not looking down on us, are ya?

17:45.355 --> 17:46.815
Y'all morons in the corps?

17:50.611 --> 17:53.238
Those eyes of yours piss me off sometimes,
you know that?

17:54.323 --> 17:56.909
You really think you're better than us,
don't ya?

18:02.873 --> 18:05.084
I vote for Aguni to be the leader.

18:06.752 --> 18:09.338
I'm pretty sure
that's what you want to hear, don't you?

18:12.883 --> 18:16.178
Well, let this be a reminder
of how you should act in the future.

18:18.430 --> 18:21.266
Hey, why are you looking so freaked out?

18:22.601 --> 18:25.312
I thought I told you
to give me an answer there?

18:26.355 --> 18:28.232
Whose side are you on, anyway?

18:30.776 --> 18:33.403
Just about to shit your pants there, huh?

18:33.487 --> 18:36.073
Look at his face!

18:38.117 --> 18:39.618
All right.

18:40.494 --> 18:42.704
Looks like we have a unanimous decision.

18:42.788 --> 18:45.332
So, we've got a new leader, right?

18:45.415 --> 18:47.501
Hatter would not allow this.

18:48.794 --> 18:51.213
If he were alive,
he would not have allowed this.

18:53.841 --> 18:55.759
But he's not alive, is he?

18:58.720 --> 19:01.849
The dead really have no say
as to what's going on. Watch.

19:04.977 --> 19:06.103
See?

19:06.728 --> 19:08.230
See?

19:10.691 --> 19:11.817
That's enough.

19:18.740 --> 19:20.200
From this day onwards,

19:21.618 --> 19:23.328
I will be the Beach's new king.

19:25.706 --> 19:28.167
Yeah, let's hear it for the King, huh?

19:33.839 --> 19:37.342
Okay, boss.
Time for the succession ceremony, right?

19:37.426 --> 19:40.345
Maybe you should open up
the black envelope.

19:50.856 --> 19:52.399
The black envelope.

19:53.817 --> 19:57.154
All the playing cards collected
by members of the Beach

19:57.946 --> 20:00.699
are kept in the safe
in Hatter's royal suite.

20:02.075 --> 20:04.620
The code for opening the safe

20:05.329 --> 20:08.749
is sealed inside the black envelope.

20:11.293 --> 20:14.087
The envelope is kept in a secret location.

20:16.506 --> 20:20.844
And the only time it's opened
is when there's a new Number 1.

20:25.807 --> 20:29.394
The new Number 1 opens the envelope
in front of the executives,

20:29.978 --> 20:32.522
but only he sees the code to the safe.

20:42.658 --> 20:45.827
Then, he places the paper
with the code written on it

20:45.911 --> 20:48.747
into a new envelope and seals it again.

20:49.498 --> 20:52.626
It then must be signed
by all the executives.

21:03.303 --> 21:05.931
First, Arisu will infiltrate
the royal suite.

21:06.598 --> 21:08.308
Then he'll search for the safe,

21:08.392 --> 21:10.686
and steal all the playing cards inside.

21:12.437 --> 21:15.440
- And how do I get the code?
- Don't worry about that.

21:16.692 --> 21:19.152
I'll let you know
when you're in front of the safe.

21:21.989 --> 21:23.448
I sure hope you're right.

21:24.449 --> 21:25.617
I'm on it.

21:27.286 --> 21:29.788
Usagi and Kuina will be on the lookout.

21:30.831 --> 21:34.376
This is too dangerous.
They'll kill us if they see us.

21:39.423 --> 21:41.842
I don't think we have any other choice.

21:43.593 --> 21:47.597
Now that Hatter's dead,
the unity in the Beach is wavering.

21:47.681 --> 21:49.391
I think this plan could work for us.

22:03.905 --> 22:05.949
I'm here to tell you,
we have a new leader.

22:07.951 --> 22:08.827
What happened?

22:08.910 --> 22:10.787
Hatter is no longer with us,

22:11.371 --> 22:13.665
and that leader has been chosen.

22:14.249 --> 22:15.667
The new leader is Aguni.

22:19.880 --> 22:21.340
Everybody, shut up!

22:23.675 --> 22:28.096
It seems as though Hatter failed
in his game. He just couldn't crack it.

22:29.139 --> 22:32.309
A vote was taken,
and the executive was unanimous,

22:32.851 --> 22:35.437
and Aguni was voted as our new Number 1.

22:37.939 --> 22:40.650
Now, let's hear from Aguni.

22:41.526 --> 22:44.237
You better all listen carefully.

22:52.788 --> 22:53.955
Niragi

22:54.039 --> 22:56.458
said everything that needs to be said.

22:58.126 --> 23:00.587
All right, the new leader
is making a speech in the lobby.

23:02.839 --> 23:05.842
All members of the executive
and the militant corps

23:05.926 --> 23:07.302
are here at the annex.

23:08.303 --> 23:10.389
We're not gonna get
another chance like this.

23:13.725 --> 23:16.436
I'll let you guys know
if there are any changes here.

23:16.520 --> 23:18.563
I'm counting on you, Arisu.

23:20.982 --> 23:21.983
Copy that.

23:27.114 --> 23:29.991
Now that Hatter is gone
and I'm the Number 1,

23:30.659 --> 23:33.412
I have full control over the Beach.

23:33.912 --> 23:37.124
Follow my orders.
I want you to live for me,

23:38.542 --> 23:40.585
and you may have to die for me.

23:54.975 --> 23:56.059
I found it.

23:57.602 --> 23:59.146
All right, what's the code?

23:59.229 --> 24:00.856
8-0-2-2.

24:01.356 --> 24:03.275
So you saw what's in the letter?

24:03.817 --> 24:04.860
No.

24:05.485 --> 24:08.071
But Aguni's expression
pretty much said it all.

24:09.364 --> 24:10.699
When he opened it,

24:11.199 --> 24:13.285
his face kinda went all dark,

24:14.578 --> 24:16.538
like he was completely surprised

24:17.289 --> 24:19.332
and really perplexed.

24:21.543 --> 24:23.670
I'm pretty sure
there was nothing written on it.

24:24.504 --> 24:26.756
Nothing? Then how did you get the code?

24:29.134 --> 24:30.802
From the wax seal.

24:31.970 --> 24:35.390
The Boss seals it with his ring.
It has numbers on it.

24:36.850 --> 24:38.643
And that's the code.

24:39.519 --> 24:41.021
8-0-2-2.

24:44.524 --> 24:46.651
Sure as hell
wouldn't want to be your enemy.

24:57.078 --> 24:58.830
It's not opening!

25:01.208 --> 25:02.417
Chishiya!

25:04.127 --> 25:05.670
Chishiya, you there?

25:08.381 --> 25:11.343
Yeah, I gotta hand it to you.
You really got balls.

25:19.017 --> 25:21.311
- Why would you…
- Let me go!

25:21.811 --> 25:24.689
- Relax, calm down!
- Usagi!

25:25.690 --> 25:26.775
Arisu!

25:26.858 --> 25:29.986
Stop crying for your boyfriend,
you stupid bitch!

25:30.070 --> 25:31.321
Arisu!

25:35.408 --> 25:37.911
Chishiya, I owe you.

25:37.994 --> 25:39.913
We wouldn't have caught them
if it wasn't for you.

25:39.996 --> 25:41.498
- Let go… Arisu!
- Yeah, well…

25:41.581 --> 25:42.749
Just wanna be of service.

25:44.251 --> 25:46.586
Stop it! Stop it!

25:56.096 --> 25:57.639
Arisu!

25:58.265 --> 26:00.475
Well, now. Looks like…

26:02.018 --> 26:03.853
Someone's gone night-night.

26:08.650 --> 26:10.944
All right. Bring him to the room.

26:28.878 --> 26:32.674
Well, rumor has it
that your visa expires tomorrow.

26:36.261 --> 26:41.182
Without your sense of hearing
or your sight, you're like a sitting duck.

26:41.766 --> 26:44.978
I can just imagine the terror
you're feeling as you sit here

26:45.061 --> 26:47.480
and wait for the laser
to burn through your skull!

26:49.566 --> 26:52.152
But for now…

26:52.235 --> 26:56.448
…I'll just enjoy all this precious time
I'm gonna have with your girlfriend.

26:58.950 --> 27:01.244
See ya!

28:01.554 --> 28:03.807
How are things going over there, Kuina?

28:05.558 --> 28:08.687
All right, I guess.
Aguni is still in his room.

28:10.355 --> 28:12.607
I'm dying of boredom over here.

28:13.942 --> 28:16.986
Well, let's go ahead with our plan, then.

28:19.406 --> 28:22.075
I have no idea
if Arisu is smart or stupid.

28:22.701 --> 28:25.453
There's no way
they'd keep the cards in an ordinary safe.

28:26.996 --> 28:29.582
Then where do you think
the real safe is?

28:30.959 --> 28:33.586
I'm not sure,
but when Arisu found the fake safe,

28:34.379 --> 28:36.923
Aguni, who usually has a good poker face,

28:37.507 --> 28:39.676
was glancing towards something else.

28:43.012 --> 28:46.349
I think that whatever's in that envelope

28:46.933 --> 28:50.145
isn't a code or some blank letter.

28:53.440 --> 28:55.984
I think it might just be a drawing.

29:19.924 --> 29:20.800
Found it.

29:21.593 --> 29:23.428
So this is
why you sacrificed them?

29:25.263 --> 29:28.850
Yeah, well, you gotta give something
to get something.

29:30.018 --> 29:33.021
They were pawns, that's all. Shit happens.

29:33.104 --> 29:36.524
Yeah, well, all I know…

29:37.567 --> 29:40.904
is that I sure as hell
wouldn't want to be your enemy.

29:42.155 --> 29:43.656
Yeah, I get that a lot.

30:48.346 --> 30:50.390
- Get your hands off me!
- Shut up!

30:50.473 --> 30:52.559
- Hurry…
- Stop struggling, man!

30:52.642 --> 30:53.643
And, heave!

30:53.726 --> 30:54.644
Now relax.

30:57.564 --> 30:59.399
- Stop resisting.
- Get off me!

31:28.970 --> 31:35.435
Rape, assault, fraud, arson, and murder.

31:36.686 --> 31:39.355
Why do you think
these things are all against the law?

31:46.237 --> 31:49.073
You tell me, why do you think
they're all against the law?

31:54.329 --> 31:56.331
Because they're all in our nature.

32:00.209 --> 32:03.796
Left to their own devices, humans will
rape, steal, and kill each other.

32:07.300 --> 32:09.052
Because that's what we're all about.

32:20.563 --> 32:23.107
But there are no laws here, are there?

32:24.275 --> 32:27.111
It's a waste to deny our basic instincts,
don't you think?

32:27.195 --> 32:29.489
I mean, it's inside us all.

32:30.156 --> 32:32.492
It even empowers us, doesn't it?

33:01.354 --> 33:02.689
Don't fuck with me.

33:06.651 --> 33:08.403
The fun is just starting.

33:32.844 --> 33:34.887
Well, I guess
I can get rid of this now, too.

33:36.139 --> 33:40.601
Don't you feel sorry for him?
Arisu, I mean.

33:41.436 --> 33:42.729
Sorry for him?

33:43.855 --> 33:46.607
Hmm. Yeah, I know I do.

33:51.571 --> 33:54.240
Sometimes we have to do things
in order to survive.

34:00.288 --> 34:03.708
If you're so worried about him,
then you should help him.

34:15.094 --> 34:16.137
No way…

34:19.057 --> 34:20.183
W-- Wait!

34:39.035 --> 34:40.078
Seriously?

35:04.060 --> 35:06.145
We would like to take this opportunity

35:06.229 --> 35:10.525
to sincerely thank you for staying
at Seaside Paradise, Tokyo.

35:10.608 --> 35:13.236
As a token of our appreciation,

35:13.319 --> 35:18.491
we will now commence a game
with all 58 participants in the venue.

35:18.574 --> 35:20.118
1 PER PERSON

35:21.953 --> 35:24.580
THE GAME WILL NOW COMMENCE

35:29.752 --> 35:30.878
The Beach is…

35:31.879 --> 35:33.172
a game arena?

35:33.756 --> 35:35.591
Difficulty,

35:35.675 --> 35:37.009
Ten of Hearts.

35:37.093 --> 35:38.052
GAME DIFFICULTY

35:39.804 --> 35:43.266
- "Ten of Hearts"!
- It happened at last.

35:46.561 --> 35:50.648
All participants
must assemble in the lobby immediately.

35:50.731 --> 35:54.026
The rules of the game
will then be explained.

35:56.028 --> 35:59.699
I repeat. All participants must assemble

35:59.782 --> 36:01.951
in the lobby immediately.

36:24.098 --> 36:26.058
Hey, there's a game
starting in the lobby!

36:26.142 --> 36:27.727
- Let's go!
- Hurry!

36:27.810 --> 36:29.979
- Quick!
- Anyone know what game it is?

36:30.062 --> 36:31.564
It's Ten of Hearts!

36:31.647 --> 36:34.066
Hurry up! Hurry, hurry. Come on!

36:34.150 --> 36:35.151
Move it!

37:15.983 --> 37:17.068
Momoka!

37:18.444 --> 37:20.988
Momoka! Why…

37:27.954 --> 37:30.706
Game, "Witch Hunt".

37:32.208 --> 37:34.877
The murderous witch who killed this girl

37:34.961 --> 37:37.296
is hiding amongst you in plain sight.

37:39.090 --> 37:42.260
The witch role is not limited to women.

37:43.469 --> 37:44.595
She's hiding here?

37:44.679 --> 37:47.390
To clear the game,
you must find the witch

37:47.473 --> 37:50.476
and burn him or her
in the Fire of Judgment.

37:51.143 --> 37:53.604
Time limit, two hours.

38:25.928 --> 38:27.805
TIME LIMIT
